  "description": "The setup wasn't complicated. Here's the pattern behind roughly 70% of my strategy... and a stock showing it right now.",
  "body_html": "<p><strong>How did I find Cheesecake Factory, <span class=\"cashtag-wrap\" data-attrs=\"{&quot;symbol&quot;:&quot;$CAKE&quot;}\" data-component-name=\"CashtagToDOM\"></span>, before it ran 62%? </strong></p><p>There is no reason to recreate the wheel. Take the strategies of the best investors and adjust them slightly to your life, risk tolerance, schedule and time frame preference. About 70% of my own strategy, is based on targeting Volatility Contraction Patterns. This is how we have been able to double and sometimes triple the performance of the S&amp;P 500. </p><p>If you have questions, leave them in the comments below, or swing by the <a href=\"https://open.substack.com/chat/posts/d18286d6-5152-4f20-85c8-cedb68ee0e71\">Main Chat</a>. </p><p class=\"button-wrapper\" data-attrs=\"{&quot;url&quot;:&quot;https://tjstocks.substack.com/subscribe?&quot;,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;Subscribe now&quot;,&quot;action&quot;:null,&quot;class&quot;:null}\" data-component-name=\"ButtonCreateButton\"><a class=\"button primary\" href=\"https://tjstocks.substack.com/subscribe?\"><span>Subscribe now</span></a></p><p>The key elements here:</p><ol><li><p>Higher lows forming, oftentimes having slightly higher highs testing a “price ceiling”</p></li><li><p>Decreasing volume leading up to the breakout.</p></li><li><p>Oftentimes an uptrend has already formed… even more reasoning why you do not need to go buy the dip or catch falling knives.</p></li><li><p>Target the breakout, as it often provides a lower risk entry. </p></li></ol><p>ALWAYS have a stop or a “cut price” in place, as a small percentage of these will fail. Control your losses, but let your winners get out of control!</p><p>For those that stuck around to the end, thank you. CVR Energy, <span class=\"cashtag-wrap\" data-attrs=\"{&quot;symbol&quot;:&quot;$CVI&quot;}\" data-component-name=\"CashtagToDOM\"></span> has a macro VCP that has formed, and is just now breaking the “price ceiling”at $44.50. A reasonable stop where this trade would be invalidated, at the lows around ~$26.75. </p><div class=\"captioned-image-container\"><figure><a class=\"image-link image2 is-viewable-img\" target=\"_blank\" href=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!sIu_!,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F7af31f80-c913-4aea-86f4-5bd51eb47031_3282x2114.png\" data-component-name=\"Image2ToDOM\"><div class=\"image2-inset\"><picture><source type=\"image/webp\" srcset=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!sIu_!,w_424,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F7af31f80-c913-4aea-86f4-5bd51eb47031_3282x2114.png 424w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!sIu_!,w_848,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F7af31f80-c913-4aea-86f4-5bd51eb47031_3282x2114.png 848w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!sIu_!,w_1272,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F7af31f80-c913-4aea-86f4-5bd51eb47031_3282x2114.png 1272w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!sIu_!,w_1456,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F7af31f80-c913-4aea-86f4-5bd51eb47031_3282x2114.png 1456w\" sizes=\"100vw\"><img src=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!sIu_!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F7af31f80-c913-4aea-86f4-5bd51eb47031_3282x2114.png\" width=\"1456\" height=\"938\" data-attrs=\"{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;https://substack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com/public/images/7af31f80-c913-4aea-86f4-5bd51eb47031_3282x2114.png&quot;,&quot;srcNoWatermark&quot;:null,&quot;fullscreen&quot;:null,&quot;imageSize&quot;:null,&quot;height&quot;:938,&quot;width&quot;:1456,&quot;resizeWidth&quot;:null,&quot;bytes&quot;:607759,&quot;alt&quot;:null,&quot;title&quot;:null,&quot;type&quot;:&quot;image/png&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:null,&quot;belowTheFold&quot;:false,&quot;topImage&quot;:true,&quot;internalRedirect&quot;:&quot;https://tjstocks.substack.com/i/214435151?img=https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F7af31f80-c913-4aea-86f4-5bd51eb47031_3282x2114.png&quot;,&quot;isProcessing&quot;:false,&quot;align&quot;:null,&quot;offset&quot;:false}\" class=\"sizing-normal\" alt=\"\" srcset=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!sIu_!,w_424,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F7af31f80-c913-4aea-86f4-5bd51eb47031_3282x2114.png 424w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!sIu_!,w_848,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F7af31f80-c913-4aea-86f4-5bd51eb47031_3282x2114.png 848w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!sIu_!,w_1272,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F7af31f80-c913-4aea-86f4-5bd51eb47031_3282x2114.png 1272w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!sIu_!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F7af31f80-c913-4aea-86f4-5bd51eb47031_3282x2114.png 1456w\" sizes=\"100vw\" fetchpriority=\"high\"></picture><div class=\"image-link-expand\"><div class=\"pencraft pc-display-flex pc-gap-8 pc-reset\"><button tabindex=\"0\" type=\"button\" class=\"pencraft pc-reset pencraft icon-container restack-image buttonBase-GK1x3M\"><svg aria-hidden=\"true\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" viewBox=\"0 0 20 20\" fill=\"none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" stroke=\"var(--color-fg-primary)\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" class=\"icon-noB79L\"><g><path d=\"M2.53001 7.81595C3.49179 4.73911 6.43281 2.5 9.91173 2.5C13.1684 2.5 15.9537 4.46214 17.0852 7.23684L17.6179 8.67647M17.6179 8.67647L18.5002 4.26471M17.6179 8.67647L13.6473 6.91176M17.4995 12.1841C16.5378 15.2609 13.5967 17.5 10.1178 17.5C6.86118 17.5 4.07589 15.5379 2.94432 12.7632L2.41165 11.3235M2.41165 11.3235L1.5293 15.7353M2.41165 11.3235L6.38224 13.0882\"></path></g></svg></button><button tabindex=\"0\" type=\"button\" class=\"pencraft pc-reset pencraft icon-container view-image buttonBase-GK1x3M\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-maximize2 lucide-maximize-2 icon-noB79L\"><polyline points=\"15 3 21 3 21 9\"></polyline><polyline points=\"9 21 3 21 3 15\"></polyline><line x1=\"21\" x2=\"14\" y1=\"3\" y2=\"10\"></line><line x1=\"3\" x2=\"10\" y1=\"21\" y2=\"14\"></line></svg></button></div></div></div></a></figure></div><p>Now I know you probably just scoffed and said: </p><p>“Tim…$26.75 is -40% away! I don’t want to risk that much!”</p><p>Very reasonable response. My retort, is to start with a smaller position size. When and if price action does in fact go up, you can build your position over time. Trend is friend. This reduces your overall portfolio risk, while getting you into a high probability winning stock. </p><p>I’ll also add, with the constant barrage of recession fears, CVR energy is a “recession resistant” stock…meaning it has the narrative catalyst to carry it higher. The earnings reports are kind of bad, with declining revenue and EPS… however, we have seen numerous stocks with terrible fundamentals, rocket. One great fundamental factor though, is that 70% of the 100M shares are closely held. So this stock is more susceptible to supply squeezes, meaning higher stock prices. </p><div class=\"captioned-image-container\"><figure><a class=\"image-link image2 is-viewable-img\